  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Mary Lazare said that the prize competition aims to identify technologies that empower caregivers and expand access to high-quality care at home, and that ACL is committed to scalable, practical solutions (s1). She later said the competition aimed to identify technologies that empower caregivers, reduce caregiver burnout, and expand access to home care (s2). She also described AI as being considered for wearables and home modifications to help people remain at home (s3), and described applying AI to caregiving, employment for people with disabilities, economic security, and connecting people to resources (s4, s5, s6, s7).",
   "sids": [
